1
00:00:14,029 --> 00:00:17,868
<i>SAWYER FARM
ESTABLISHED 1845

2
00:00:19,494 --> 00:00:28,548
<i># Happy birthday to you...

3
00:00:28,672 --> 00:00:33,513
<i># Happy birthday, dear Jed...

4
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:38,434
<i># Happy birthday to you...

5
00:00:38,559 --> 00:00:40,271
All right, now make a wish.

6
00:00:40,306 --> 00:00:41,273
Blow them out.

7
00:00:46,068 --> 00:00:48,321
Yes! Very good!

8
00:00:48,362 --> 00:00:50,532
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

9
00:00:50,573 --> 00:00:51,784
Very good!

10
00:00:51,908 --> 00:00:53,202
All right...

11
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:59,086
Drayton, where are your manners?

12
00:00:59,169 --> 00:01:01,338
Give the first slice to the thief.

13
00:01:16,105 --> 00:01:17,586
I didn't steal your damn pigs...

14
00:01:17,621 --> 00:01:19,068
Are you calling my son a liar?

15
00:01:19,193 --> 00:01:21,446
He saw your filthy hands stealing our property...

16
00:01:26,032 --> 00:01:28,829
Why would I go anywhere near your filthy pigs?

17
00:01:28,953 --> 00:01:30,415
Or your filthy family!

18
00:01:30,498 --> 00:01:33,585
I swear, everybody will know what kind of...

19
00:01:33,626 --> 00:01:35,504
...offspring you're raising here, Verna!

20
00:01:35,586 --> 00:01:37,423
Shut him up! I've had enough!

21
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,933
Listen to me, no farmhand is going to...

22
00:01:40,968 --> 00:01:42,764
...ruin my son's special night.

23
00:01:46,017 --> 00:01:47,394
Ready for your present?

24
00:01:50,689 --> 00:01:52,692
You know you're my special boy.

25
00:01:53,275 --> 00:01:55,362
Come on, Jed. There you go...

26
00:01:58,199 --> 00:02:00,452
- Jed.
- Yes, that's it, Jed.

27
00:02:02,955 --> 00:02:03,999
Now remember,

28
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:07,336
bad people like him try to destroy our family.

29
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:09,756
But we won't let that happen, will we?

30
00:02:09,922 --> 00:02:11,298
Go on, pick it up...

31
00:02:12,091 --> 00:02:13,593
Jed, pick it up...

32
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:14,970
Jed!

33
00:02:15,094 --> 00:02:18,723
Jed...

34
00:02:18,764 --> 00:02:20,310
Pick it up, Jed!

35
00:02:20,351 --> 00:02:23,647
Jed!

36
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,441
Come on, you know what you have to do...

37
00:02:26,858 --> 00:02:28,571
That's it, Jed!

38
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:31,991
Come on, Jed...

39
00:02:32,699 --> 00:02:35,537
Jed!

40
00:02:35,619 --> 00:02:37,080
No!

41
00:02:37,121 --> 00:02:38,374
There you go.

42
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:40,042
Go on, son!

43
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:41,378
No!

44
00:02:48,092 --> 00:02:49,804
No!

45
00:02:55,394 --> 00:02:57,481
No!

46
00:02:57,647 --> 00:02:59,483
No, please!

47
00:02:59,608 --> 00:03:02,403
No!

48
00:03:02,444 --> 00:03:05,073
Do it, do it, do it!

49
00:03:05,114 --> 00:03:07,075
No!

50
00:03:07,116 --> 00:03:08,827
Go on, Jed, do it...

51
00:03:09,786 --> 00:03:10,830
Do it!

52
00:03:11,414 --> 00:03:13,626
- Jed.
- Do it!

53
00:03:19,923 --> 00:03:21,051
Mom!

54
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,094
Mom, no!

55
00:03:24,846 --> 00:03:28,185
No!

56
00:03:38,071 --> 00:03:38,906
Hey.

57
00:03:39,197 --> 00:03:40,784
You let us down, Jed.

58
00:03:43,536 --> 00:03:46,623
It's all right. Family will always be here for
you.

59
00:03:46,789 --> 00:03:48,124
Remember that.

60
00:03:48,875 --> 00:03:49,918
All right.

61
00:04:07,606 --> 00:04:12,697
<i>TEXAS, 1955

62
00:04:15,698 --> 00:04:17,119
Are you trying to get us killed?

63
00:04:17,159 --> 00:04:18,036
Do you want me to stop?

64
00:04:18,078 --> 00:04:19,329
No, I didn't say that.

65
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:27,716
Watch out!

66
00:04:32,429 --> 00:04:34,225
What the hell was that thing?

67
00:04:35,516 --> 00:04:36,728
Hey, Betty.

68
00:04:43,943 --> 00:04:45,195
What is it?

69
00:04:46,487 --> 00:04:47,615
I don't know.

70
00:04:50,868 --> 00:04:52,330
Then let's go.

71
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:02,592
What?

72
00:05:10,976 --> 00:05:12,312
He's just a kid!

73
00:05:14,356 --> 00:05:15,650
Let's go!

74
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:17,443
We'll be late.

75
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:21,072
Hello.

76
00:05:25,328 --> 00:05:26,622
Are you okay?

77
00:05:32,753 --> 00:05:34,798
You shouldn't play in the road.

78
00:05:34,964 --> 00:05:36,925
Help me, please...

79
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:45,061
Hey, Betty, where are you going? I didn't hit him!

80
00:05:45,477 --> 00:05:47,105
- Something's wrong.
- Betty!

81
00:05:47,145 --> 00:05:48,565
He needs help.

82
00:05:49,107 --> 00:05:50,525
Jesus Christ!

83
00:05:54,947 --> 00:05:56,909
Hey, buddy, can you hear me?

84
00:05:58,911 --> 00:06:00,454
Let me help you!

85
00:06:04,332 --> 00:06:05,501
Hello?

86
00:06:12,133 --> 00:06:14,722
It's okay. You can come out.

87
00:06:16,179 --> 00:06:17,308
Betty.

88
00:06:21,103 --> 00:06:22,814
Betty, where did you go?

89
00:07:21,094 --> 00:07:22,389
Hello?

90
00:07:27,561 --> 00:07:31,107
Come on... I won't hurt you.

91
00:07:33,650 --> 00:07:35,153
I just want to help...

92
00:07:42,203 --> 00:07:43,372
Okay?

93
00:07:54,261 --> 00:07:58,558
<i>BASED ON CHARACTERS CREATED BY

94
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:01,604
<i>KIM HENKEL AND TOBE HOOPER

95
00:08:03,897 --> 00:08:05,941
You did good, Jed!

96
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:09,779
It's like... I can still feel you in there
after all.

97
00:08:41,107 --> 00:08:44,696
Well, let him learn a little more.

98
00:08:48,157 --> 00:08:49,702
Oh, my God!

99
00:08:59,338 --> 00:09:00,257
Show him!

100
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,857
- Where is she?
- Calm down, Hal.

101
00:09:15,357 --> 00:09:16,944
Let me through, damn it!

102
00:09:16,985 --> 00:09:18,530
Let me go! Let me go, damn it!

103
00:09:18,570 --> 00:09:20,155
- We know what happened.
- Calm down, Hal.

104
00:09:20,321 --> 00:09:21,950
Is that my little girl in there?

105
00:09:23,451 --> 00:09:26,330
Is she in there? Is my little girl in there?

106
00:09:26,664 --> 00:09:28,041
Answer me, damn it!

107
00:09:28,374 --> 00:09:29,751
We've got one of them.

108
00:09:34,130 --> 00:09:35,509
Oh, boy!

109
00:09:39,679 --> 00:09:41,057
I couldn't get to her in time!

110
00:09:41,265 --> 00:09:43,310
I'm so sorry, sir. I swear to God.

111
00:09:45,811 --> 00:09:47,522
Drayton Sawyer...

112
00:09:50,024 --> 00:09:51,903
It's time to go to Gorman Reformatory.

113
00:09:51,944 --> 00:09:55,283
No... You're all grown up now.

114
00:09:57,534 --> 00:09:59,538
That means the gas chamber for you.

115
00:10:03,208 --> 00:10:04,462
Why?

116
00:10:04,794 --> 00:10:06,631
Are you going to arrest me for finding a dead
body?

117
00:10:06,838 --> 00:10:08,300
Last I checked, that wasn't a crime.

118
00:10:08,349 --> 00:10:11,103
How about a bullet hole in your damn skull?

119
00:10:11,769 --> 00:10:13,069
- Put it away, Hal.
- Come on.

120
00:10:13,104 --> 00:10:14,982
He's right. We've got nothing on him...

121
00:10:15,356 --> 00:10:16,565
Calm down, Hal.

122
00:10:16,773 --> 00:10:17,525
Keep your head clear.

123
00:10:17,565 --> 00:10:20,069
- Hal, it's not worth it.
- Come on, Hal, lower the gun.

124
00:10:20,193 --> 00:10:21,529
Damn trash.

125
00:10:32,705 --> 00:10:34,666
Let those boys go right this instant!

126
00:10:34,957 --> 00:10:36,626
Don't count on it, Verna!

127
00:10:37,376 --> 00:10:38,837
Do you think they did anything wrong?

128
00:10:38,877 --> 00:10:39,963
No, I don't!

129
00:10:40,045 --> 00:10:41,881
You bastard, let them out of the car!

130
00:10:42,381 --> 00:10:45,176
No! They're going to stay there and rot!

131
00:10:46,259 --> 00:10:47,344
On what charges?

132
00:10:47,635 --> 00:10:48,929
They're not under arrest.

133
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:51,265
They're in protective custody... from you.

134
00:10:51,306 --> 00:10:52,558
What are you talking about?

135
00:10:53,558 --> 00:10:56,103
I can't count how many crime scenes I've been
to...

136
00:10:56,144 --> 00:10:58,481
...where there's always a Sawyer involved.

137
00:10:59,023 --> 00:11:00,816
Those boys aren't safe with you...

138
00:11:00,898 --> 00:11:02,026
Bullshit.

139
00:11:02,942 --> 00:11:05,280
Get a warrant for the Sawyer house.

140
00:11:05,612 --> 00:11:07,657
Name every one of them. I want them all.

141
00:11:07,823 --> 00:11:08,825
- Did you hear me?
- You can't do that.

142
00:11:08,907 --> 00:11:09,784
You can't do that!

143
00:11:09,867 --> 00:11:11,578
Well, by the time we get there, I'll have a
warrant saying I can...

144
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:13,121
...do just that.

145
00:11:13,787 --> 00:11:15,914
It's called "children at risk."

146
00:11:17,332 --> 00:11:19,293
You took one of mine...

147
00:11:20,043 --> 00:11:22,463
...so I'll take every one of yours, Verna.

148
00:11:28,635 --> 00:11:30,011
Every last one of them...

149
00:11:32,013 --> 00:11:34,016
<i>10 YEARS LATER

150
00:11:34,474 --> 00:11:38,145
<i>In 1935, the state of Texas established a...

151
00:11:38,186 --> 00:11:40,689
<i>...program to care for children at risk.

152
00:11:40,855 --> 00:11:44,193
In its first year, nearly 52 children were
removed from homes...

153
00:11:44,274 --> 00:11:47,111
...known to be involved in criminal activity.

154
00:11:47,444 --> 00:11:50,324
<i>Many of these children were given new names...

155
00:11:50,365 --> 00:11:52,159
<i>...and placed in foster homes.

156
00:11:52,283 --> 00:11:55,871
<i>Others, products of degenerate parenting...

157
00:11:55,912 --> 00:11:58,749
<i>...ended up here at Gorman Reformatory.

158
00:11:58,790 --> 00:12:00,165
<i>GORMAN HOUSE JUVENILE REFORMATORY

159
00:12:00,206 --> 00:12:04,336
We take care of their physical and
psychological needs.

160
00:12:04,794 --> 00:12:06,047
Yes, sir.

161
00:12:06,171 --> 00:12:08,967
I've wanted to come here for a long time.

162
00:12:09,257 --> 00:12:10,593
I think I can help them.

163
00:12:10,759 --> 00:12:11,803
Elizabeth.

164
00:12:11,843 --> 00:12:13,471
Please, sir, Lizzy. Lizzy is fine.

165
00:12:13,512 --> 00:12:15,013
Elizabeth.

166
00:12:15,972 --> 00:12:18,225
Most of these children will end up...

167
00:12:18,265 --> 00:12:20,477
...in prisons or mental institutions.

168
00:12:21,519 --> 00:12:24,983
Keeping them here makes everyone safer.

169
00:12:25,774 --> 00:12:27,026
Keep your guard up.

170
00:13:11,694 --> 00:13:13,071
Well... hello...

171
00:13:13,904 --> 00:13:15,365
My name is Lizzy.

172
00:13:15,448 --> 00:13:18,327
I'm new here, and I'd like to get to know you.

173
00:13:22,872 --> 00:13:24,207
That's Bud.

174
00:13:25,833 --> 00:13:28,209
He doesn't say much for such a big guy.

175
00:13:33,632 --> 00:13:34,634
You're in my seat.

176
00:13:35,175 --> 00:13:36,344
I'm sorry.

177
00:13:37,218 --> 00:13:39,221
- Very nice.
- I'm...

178
00:13:39,262 --> 00:13:41,307
Lizzy... Yeah, I heard. I heard.

179
00:13:42,306 --> 00:13:44,476
Shit, sorry. I'm Jackson.

180
00:13:45,267 --> 00:13:48,230
Jackson and... Bud...

181
00:13:49,022 --> 00:13:51,484
And what medication are you taking, Jackson?

182
00:13:51,650 --> 00:13:52,860
Medication?

183
00:13:54,069 --> 00:13:56,030
They already gave it to us when they brought
us in, right?

184
00:13:57,029 --> 00:13:59,949
We figured you'd know more about that than we
do, Lizzy...

185
00:14:00,949 --> 00:14:03,371
You're not going to give me any trouble, are you?

186
00:14:03,870 --> 00:14:05,331
No, not me, Lizzy.

187
00:14:06,665 --> 00:14:07,964
Is there a reason you keep...

188
00:14:07,999 --> 00:14:09,543
...saying my name like that?

189
00:14:10,126 --> 00:14:14,380
No... I just like to know who's in charge,
that's all.

190
00:14:17,465 --> 00:14:19,135
Fuck you, asshole!

191
00:14:19,176 --> 00:14:20,095
I'll kick your ass.

192
00:14:20,135 --> 00:14:21,888
I'll fuck up your head!

193
00:14:22,012 --> 00:14:23,098
Let him go!

194
00:14:23,138 --> 00:14:24,683
Mind your own business!

195
00:14:24,807 --> 00:14:26,190
It is my business.

196
00:14:26,225 --> 00:14:27,643
What's the problem?

197
00:14:28,142 --> 00:14:30,562
He said something I didn't like.

198
00:14:30,853 --> 00:14:34,358
About what a girl in a nurse's uniform would
taste like.

199
00:14:35,233 --> 00:14:36,820
Hey, hey, let go of me!

200
00:14:37,111 --> 00:14:38,488
Let go!

201
00:14:39,321 --> 00:14:40,907
Fuck you, Frankenstein!

202
00:14:40,948 --> 00:14:42,574
That's enough. Stop it.

203
00:14:42,949 --> 00:14:45,370
- Ike, what did you do?
- I didn't do anything.

204
00:14:48,414 --> 00:14:49,624
Everything's fine.

205
00:15:50,599 --> 00:15:52,226
What are you doing?

206
00:15:57,188 --> 00:15:58,482
Come here.

207
00:16:01,818 --> 00:16:03,321
What's the problem?

208
00:16:03,362 --> 00:16:05,198
It's just a stupid mouse.

209
00:16:08,075 --> 00:16:09,369
Got a light?

210
00:16:09,451 --> 00:16:11,286
You know smoking isn't allowed in here...

211
00:16:13,579 --> 00:16:15,958
I have special permission.

212
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:18,002
True story.

213
00:16:18,043 --> 00:16:19,963
Ask Dr. Lang.

214
00:16:20,170 --> 00:16:21,005
I will.

215
00:16:21,046 --> 00:16:23,007
He'll tell you it helps me.

216
00:16:24,091 --> 00:16:26,717
With my anxiety.

217
00:16:29,970 --> 00:16:31,514
The truth is...

218
00:16:32,555 --> 00:16:34,685
...it's because I'm his favorite.

219
00:16:35,059 --> 00:16:36,521
He told me so.

220
00:16:36,728 --> 00:16:39,398
- You've earned yourself a warning.
- Why?

221
00:16:39,438 --> 00:16:40,983
I was just taking a bath.

222
00:16:41,023 --> 00:16:42,359
Get out.

223
00:16:45,778 --> 00:16:47,072
Bitch.

224
00:16:48,906 --> 00:16:50,660
Is everything all right?

225
00:16:51,368 --> 00:16:53,579
Yes, Doctor, I'm fine.

226
00:16:54,161 --> 00:16:59,042
I'll handle Isaac and Bud.

227
00:16:59,125 --> 00:17:00,877
No. Bud didn't do anything.

228
00:17:00,918 --> 00:17:03,317
I look forward to our session tomorrow, Jackson.

229
00:17:03,352 --> 00:17:05,716
I'm sorry, but he's actually right.

230
00:17:05,756 --> 00:17:07,051
Bud didn't do anything.

231
00:17:07,092 --> 00:17:09,218
He was fighting...

232
00:17:09,843 --> 00:17:11,512
Well, he was protecting me...

233
00:17:11,594 --> 00:17:12,847
Remind me to tell you later what...

234
00:17:12,887 --> 00:17:14,473
...he did to his last foster family.

235
00:17:14,556 --> 00:17:16,225
Well, they took his dog away.

236
00:17:16,766 --> 00:17:20,062
Yes... that's a perfectly good reason...

237
00:17:20,103 --> 00:17:22,732
...to put someone in a coma.

238
00:17:23,107 --> 00:17:24,608
Well, I'm just saying.

239
00:17:47,046 --> 00:17:47,964
<i>DIAGNOSIS: BIPOLAR DISORDER

240
00:17:48,005 --> 00:17:51,926
<i>Upon admission, this 16-year-old boy,
Horton, Bud, was depressed, agitated and
fearful.

241
00:17:52,051 --> 00:17:55,094
<i>Overall, his behavior was aggressive,
unusually energetic and withdrawn.

242
00:17:58,306 --> 00:18:00,142
Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

243
00:18:00,892 --> 00:18:02,227
You didn't.

244
00:18:02,977 --> 00:18:04,563
Thank you for helping Bud.

245
00:18:05,647 --> 00:18:09,275
I know you don't even know him, so that was nice.

246
00:18:10,025 --> 00:18:12,945
Well, I'm here to help you all. So...

247
00:18:14,697 --> 00:18:16,992
You're the first pretty nurse we've had around
here.

248
00:18:19,869 --> 00:18:21,455
So I thought you should know...

249
00:18:22,956 --> 00:18:24,124
Know what?

250
00:18:24,457 --> 00:18:27,087
What goes on in the relaxation room...

251
00:18:28,003 --> 00:18:29,882
The kids around here call it...

252
00:18:30,048 --> 00:18:32,301
...Dr. Lang's chamber of horrors.

253
00:18:32,717 --> 00:18:34,303
Piece of shit.

254
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:36,138
Why is that?

255
00:18:36,513 --> 00:18:39,014
Go there at night and find out for yourself...

256
00:18:40,556 --> 00:18:43,060
Hey, you might even do something about it.

257
00:18:44,435 --> 00:18:45,521
You know.

258
00:18:46,689 --> 00:18:47,816
Jackson...

259
00:18:50,109 --> 00:18:52,277
You'll get out of here one day.

260
00:18:52,568 --> 00:18:55,197
And just because you can't trust certain people...

261
00:18:56,698 --> 00:18:58,826
...doesn't mean you shouldn't trust others.

262
00:18:59,909 --> 00:19:01,537
Well, I'll think about it.

263
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,419
<i>DR. LANG

264
00:19:13,006 --> 00:19:14,508
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

265
00:19:14,590 --> 00:19:17,261
Barry Farnsworth, we had an appointment an
hour ago.

266
00:19:17,343 --> 00:19:18,762
Did we?

267
00:19:21,056 --> 00:19:22,598
Mrs. Sawyer.

268
00:19:22,764 --> 00:19:24,934
It's Mrs. Carson now.

269
00:19:31,023 --> 00:19:32,608
I want to see Jed.

270
00:19:32,941 --> 00:19:35,028
We've been through this before.

271
00:19:35,527 --> 00:19:36,904
Year after year...

272
00:19:36,945 --> 00:19:38,281
He's my son.

273
00:19:38,697 --> 00:19:40,325
And I can afford a lawyer now.

274
